    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a1">

                <pb facs="0418" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Dufferin to Sir Edward Thornton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Citadel, Quebec, Canada</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 9, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: My government has had under consideration
                    Mr. Drummond’s dispatch of the 6th August last and its inclosures, regarding the
                    regulations governing the transportation of dutiable merchandise between the
                    United States and Canada, and I have now the honor of communicating to you a
                    report of a committee of the privy council recommending that the regulations
                    contained in the circular of the Secretary of the United States Treasury of the
                    15th September and 27th November, 1876, be approved and confirmed.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DUFFERIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
